      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The delay you're experiencing is due to DNS propagation, which is essentially how the internet updates its records across various servers worldwide. It can take anywhere from a few minutes to 48 hours for all of these servers to recognize your new A record. You can't force it to update instantly, but you can check the current status using online DNS lookup tools to see how far the change has spread. For the most immediate results, you might try flushing the DNS cache on your local machine or the client's network devices.",
