    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. so it's mostly just the ttl and all that caching stuff right? i was hoping there was some kind of command to force the updates to happen faster on the provider side. is there anything else that could be causing the inconsistency besides just waiting it out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, the Time To Live (TTL) setting is the primary factor dictating how long caches hold onto the old information, which is why you're seeing this lag. You can't generally issue a command to the DNS provider to bypass their caching mechanisms; it's a distributed system, not a single-file update. If you want to speed up future changes, you could temporarily lower the TTL on your records before making an update, but be warned, this makes *all* future changes more frequent and potentially more resource-intensive. It's less about forcing the update and more about telling the world to forget the old IP faster.",
      "source": "target",
