      "content": "It's highly unlikely that the records are actually getting \"lost\" or corrupted during propagation, though the inconsistency certainly feels that way to the users! When you see some users succeeding and others failing, it's almost always because their local resolver or ISP's cache is still holding onto the old, stale data. Think of it like a swarm of little, slightly confused delivery drivers—some have the new map, and some are still following the old, dusty route. The process isn't corruption; it's just a staggered rollout across the global network.",
